    {
      "id": "yc4y4rq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Energy is defined as the capacity of a body to do work and is a scalar quantity.",
        "Kinetic Energy is the energy possessed by an object due to its motion (KE = 1/2 m v²).",
        "Potential Energy is the stored energy in an object due to its position or shape (PE = mgh).",
        "The Law of Conservation of Energy states that energy can neither be created nor destroyed, only transformed.",
        "Power is the rate at which work is done or energy is consumed (P = Work / Time)."
      ],
      "id": "s6h4344"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6ovn0rl",
      "content": "• Energy is the capacity to do work."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z5khy1d",
      "content": "• Energy can exist in different forms such as mechanical energy, heat energy, electrical energy and chemical energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ohj7gfp",
      "content": "• The SI unit of energy is Joule (J)."
    },
    {
      "id": "6am0xvq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Forms of Energy"
    },
