    {
      "id": "ezc1yhr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Law of Conservation of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3728zs7",
      "content": "The law of conservation of energy states that energy can neither be created nor destroyed; it can only be converted from one form to another."
    },
    {
      "id": "s1ar9m8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Mechanical Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3pf26i0",
      "content": "Mechanical energy is the sum of kinetic energy and potential energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w7h8vxx",
      "content": "Mechanical Energy = KE + PE"
    },
    {
      "id": "y8uoaz6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Meaning of Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0lp4qbv",
      "content": "Power is the rate at which work is done or energy is transferred."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "au4i7az",
      "content": "Formula: Power = Work / Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iywcz3i",
      "content": "SI Unit of Power = Watt (W)"
    },
    {
      "id": "uzep8qf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Units of Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Doubling the velocity of a moving object increases its Kinetic Energy by a factor of 4.",
        "Kilowatt-hour (kWh) is the commercial unit of electrical energy, NOT power.",
        "1 Horsepower (HP) is equal to exactly 746 Watts.",
        "Total Mechanical Energy (KE + PE) of a freely falling body remains constant at all points."
      ],
      "id": "fz6drkc"
    },
